      "writtenOn": "2025-02-11T18:19:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this primarily affects SCHED_NORMAL tasks that use the pi-futexes (as well as in-kernel rt-mutex contention between SCHED_NORMAL tasks). \n\nProxy-Exec currently resloves normal mutex priority inversion. So the need for in-kerenel use of rt-mutexes would decline, but proxy-exec currently isn\u0027t connected to futex behavior, so it can\u0027t yet help there.\n\nSo this is for the moment complementary, as while its not as deep a solution as proxy-exec, it covers some of the cases proxy-exec doesn\u0027t yet address.",
      "parentUuid": "8343b2df_bec558f8",
      "revId": "b7adb05f753fb338ffd2517a3390946df02ce59a",
